  "description": "NOCBOX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C89 H70 Br8 N13 Nd5 O34,2(H2 O1),3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 4 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 10 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a chain with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.660-3.940 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.79-113.51°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd5L4(OH)2(NO3)5MeOH]·3MeOH·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 5 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 5 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
